WEBVTT

NOTE Ruwaidix source-grounded narration; original owner archive and labeled explanations.

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.493
Under a microscope, a zebrafish embryo can look

00:00:03.493 --> 00:00:04.126
remarkably

00:00:04.126 --> 00:00:07.893
clear. Cutting a useful series of sections is another

00:00:07.893 --> 00:00:08.533
matter. A

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:12.095
small turn can change which anatomy a blade will

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:12.540
reach.

00:00:17.145 --> 00:00:20.933
I wanted to hold each specimen at the right angle

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:21.397
before

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:24.280
embedding it for histology. Two-percent agarose

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.262
offered a way to

00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:26.808
keep that orientation fixed.

00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:34.343
After processing, paraffin was supposed to support the

00:00:34.343 --> 00:00:34.682
block

00:00:34.682 --> 00:00:37.820
through the microtome. The workflow looked reasonable

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:38.234
because

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:41.341
each material solved a different practical problem.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.504
But when the blade met the block, it did not produce

00:00:49.504 --> 00:00:50.270
the ribbon

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.736
I needed. Two layers separated, and fragments

00:00:52.736 --> 00:00:53.558
collected where

00:00:53.558 --> 00:00:55.385
interpretable sections should have been.

00:00:59.312 --> 00:01:02.475
The problem was not a dramatic malfunction of the

00:01:02.475 --> 00:01:03.121
microtome.

00:01:03.121 --> 00:01:05.787
What failed was the material assembly that

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:08.453
the machine had been given to cut.

00:01:12.145 --> 00:01:15.235
Agarose is water-loving; paraffin is not. Their

00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:15.827
different

00:01:15.827 --> 00:01:19.019
behavior offers a plausible explanation for the

00:01:19.019 --> 00:01:19.970
interface, but

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.433
my photographs alone cannot prove the exact failure

00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:24.112
mechanism.

00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:31.451
Changing the agarose grade, processing conditions, or

00:01:31.451 --> 00:01:31.920
embedding

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.607
strategy might have answered it. I did not establish

00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:35.962
which

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:39.656
correction would work, and I will not call the attempt

00:01:39.656 --> 00:01:40.408
successful.

00:01:44.895 --> 00:01:48.357
I kept the photographs because they describe a real

00:01:48.357 --> 00:01:49.171
outcome: the

00:01:49.171 --> 00:01:52.605
specimen never became a usable section. An experiment

00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:53.058
can end

00:01:53.058 --> 00:01:56.168
before the measurement it was designed to produce.
